# WolkaraForever layer patch 0043 - authorization: name every blocked state
#
# Why: when the developer service could not prepare a launch, the helper either
# replied nothing at all or with free text, so the app could only say "provider
# status unavailable" for a device that was simply not enrolled. Each refusal now
# carries a state the launch UI can turn into one actionable sentence, and a
# missing device identifier is a reply rather than silence. No new permission,
# fallback or weaker check is introduced: every path still refuses.
# Needs: authorization/App/AuthorizationBlockedState.{h,m} from the layer.
# Applies to: authorization/Tunnel/PacketServiceProbe.swift,
#             authorization/Tunnel/LocalPacketProvider.m,
#             authorization/App/LocalAuthorization.{h,m}
# Upstream: candidate (not submitted).
#
